-- Which database holds issue #7's element? Walk the owner chain up to the
-- WORLD: a PDMS world is named after its database, so the last Q NAME answers
-- it without guessing at a query keyword.
--
-- refno prefix 24381 is already known to be dbnum 7997 (*MASTER/HVAC): the
-- 157257 pe rows under that prefix match dbnum_info_table's 7997 row exactly.
-- 24383 belongs to a design DB that has never been parsed, because the MDB in
-- use (/ALL1) carries only 7997.
--
-- One ALPHA LOG per section: ALPHA LOG buffers until END, so a failing command
-- discards everything still unflushed.
--
-- Keep every "--" at the start of its own line: PML treats it as a comment
-- opener anywhere on a line.

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/codex_dbof_a.log" OVER
$P SECTION_A_ALIVE
ALPHA LOG END

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/codex_dbof_b.log" OVER
$P SECTION_B_CAP_24383_66460_OWNER_CHAIN
=24383/66460
Q TYPE
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
ALPHA LOG END

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/codex_dbof_c.log" OVER
$P SECTION_C_PANEL_24381_35844_OWNER_CHAIN
=24381/35844
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
OWNER
Q TYPE
Q NAME
ALPHA LOG END
